// The Go side of the UTF-8 benchmarks.
//
// This is the fairest comparison in the suite. unicode/utf8 is pure computation
// over a byte slice, with no allocator, no interface dispatch and no runtime
// underneath it, so the two implementations are doing the same table lookups
// and the same compares on the same bytes. A gap here is burrow's to explain.
//
// One row looks like it is not a fair fight and it is the interesting one. Go's
// range loop is generated by the compiler, inline, with no call per rune, and a
// C port that spells the same loop out of two functions has an obvious way to
// lose. RangeMixed against utf8_range_mixed is the row worth reading first, and
// it is the row that made burrow change.
//
// ValidLong is the other one to read. Both sides skip a machine word at a time
// through a run of ASCII, so it is measuring the same idea written twice.
//
